# The board's power tuning lives in rc files at the root of the image, and the
# platform labels the root by name: /fstab.*, /init.*, /ueventd.* are spelled
# out in plat_file_contexts and nothing else is. power.mocha.rc and power.tn8.rc
# match none of those patterns, so the image builder finds no label for them and
# refuses to write the image at all:
#
#   set_selinux_xattr: No such file or directory searching for label
#   "/power.mocha.rc"
#
# This is the short way out. The long one is moving these files to
# /vendor/etc/init/hw, where Q expects a board's rc files and where init picks
# them up without being told; when that happens this file goes away with them.
/power\..*\.rc          u:object_r:rootfs:s0
